# Keep the build context to what actually compiles the binaries: go.mod,
# go.sum, cmd/ and internal/. Everything else is either a secret, a build
# artefact, or documentation.

.git/
.gitignore

# Secrets — never in a build context, even though no Dockerfile copies them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# The Flutter client: ~900 MB of build output, and no Go binary needs it.
app/

# Not needed to build.
docs/
.github/
deploy/
bin/
dist/
*.md

# The classifier's prompt is a .md file that the binary embeds. Excluding it
# makes the build fail with "contains no embeddable files", which is a
# confusing way to learn that a prompt is source code rather than prose.
!internal/classify/prompts/
!internal/classify/prompts/*.md
data/archive/
data/raw/
